  "title": "Same Tree",
  "slug": "same-tree",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "description": "Given the roots of two binary trees p and q, write a function to check if they are the same or not.\nTwo binary trees are considered the same if they are structurally identical, and the nodes have the same value.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "example_num": 1,
      "example_text": "Input: p = [1,2,3], q = [1,2,3]\nOutput: true"
    },
    {
      "example_num": 2,
      "example_text": "Input: p = [1,2], q = [1,null,2]\nOutput: false"
    },
    {
      "example_num": 3,
      "example_text": "Input: p = [1,2,1], q = [1,1,2]\nOutput: false"
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "The number of nodes in both trees is in the range [0, 100].",
    "-104 <= Node.val <= 104"
  ],
